# Private Utility Auth Buttons

When a Google-auth private utility has `#signInBtn` and `#signOutBtn`, update both on every auth state change. Showing the email while leaving Sign in visible is a recurring bug.

Required helper (same as Recipe Book / KCRW / Expense Helper / Travel):

```js
function setSignedInUi(isSignedIn) {
  signInBtn.hidden = isSignedIn;
  signOutBtn.hidden = !isSignedIn;
  signInBtn.style.display = isSignedIn ? "none" : "";
  signOutBtn.style.display = isSignedIn ? "" : "none";
}
```

Call it from `onAuthStateChanged` for signed-in, signed-out, and unauthorized. Setting `userLabel` is not enough. Keep both `hidden` and `style.display` because `button { display: inline-flex }` can override `[hidden]` in apps that lack `!important`.
